      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits at the western end of the forested Penteli mountain range, averaging 308 m above sea level.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nea_Erythraia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early 20th‑century refugee houses, including double residences built for widows and orphans in 1928, still line Nea Erythraia’s streets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/nea_erythraia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Kifisos river marks Nea Erythraia’s northwestern border, flowing through the suburb’s green spaces.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nea_Erythraia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Nea Erythraia’s built‑up area blends seamlessly with neighboring Kifisia, creating a continuous residential corridor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
